Episode: Receptor & Reason 2026-09-15 - verification: one ECoG array decodes simultaneous speech and gesture in three BRAVO participants and held-out pairings decode as well as trained ones, so the decoders compose rather than memorize, with context-inclusive training required; surprisal difference is attenuated across the schizophrenia spectrum in 144 Turkish speakers and embedding intrinsic dimensionality is reduced in the severe groups, but the two ID estimators disagree on sign (+0.27 vs -0.45); K-Bench measures clinician agreement (89% overall, 75% severity, 66% suicide) before calibrating a judge to 94% consensus across 125 configurations and 200 risk vignettes, and finds elevated reasoning buys no safety; 26 LLMs fabricate 55% of biomedical references with ~15% correct in every field and same-family models diverging 79% vs 29% on author accuracy; AutoScreen lifts MUC1, PDPN and LRRC15 from ranks 118/81/1384 to 5/44/659 with all three validated in primary human NK assays and names auditability over accuracy as the prerequisite; Emet nominates two-target combinations for squamous lung from a 1.5-billion-triple graph and goes two-for-four with CDC7/PKMYT1 synergy; HypoEvolve makes agent collaboration the manipulated variable and gains most where pretraining exposure is hardest to exclude; 23,015 of 91,644 BindingDB Ki labels sit at exactly pKi 5.00 and the authors decline to call their calibration a Ki-to-IC50 conversion; FAERS anti-amyloid/aspirin ARIA signals appear in three of four models while the lecanemab/tPA haemorrhage signal rests on five reports; AppSAA mice show vascular amyloid by 8 months and no cortical sex effect; MDMA cuts ethanol intake in msP rats via central amygdala and not VTA; and placebo hunger expectations reorganize resting-state prefrontal coupling in 60 women with no task present
